From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hans2294 <22217531+hans2294@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:02:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] linuxkpi: Mappings fault their pages in, so buffers can move

A mapping was made once and for all, and unmap_mapping_range() did nothing, so
a program kept writing to the old place when a buffer moved: to other buffers'
memory, or freed RAM. Now a mapping is a VMCache whose Fault() runs Linux's
fault handler and maps pages from the vma's table, and unmap_mapping_range()
empties the table and the page tables in all teams. Teams that exit or crash
no longer leave their mappings behind.

vramlimit and vis_vramlimit in the driver's settings make a big card small for
testing, and evicttest moves mapped buffers while it writes to them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
